# Switched by a script on tick 2, and still switched twenty ticks later. This
# is the defect: the Advance phase read the node's `animation` property every
# tick and put the clip back, so the documented script route did nothing.
tick 20 /Stage var:clip == burst

# The property carries what is playing, so the two routes are one route and a
# save round-trips to the same animation.
tick 20 /Stage/Fx animation == burst

# A finished non-looping clip went back to its first frame rather than sitting
# on its last one for the life of the node.
tick 39 /Stage var:replays == 2
tick 39 /Stage var:frame == 0
